! A magnetic iodine atom in a box, with spin-orbit coupling and a
! fully-relativistic PAW dataset: the cell that reaches `PAW_potential`'s
! `with_small_so` branch.
!
! The all-electron partial waves of a Dirac solution carry a small component
! beside the large one, and the small component's magnetization points along the
! radial direction, so it enters the one-centre exchange-correlation as a
! projector on `r-hat` rather than as a number. QE enters that branch when the
! dataset is fully relativistic and the density has magnetization channels,
! which is `has_so .AND. nspin_mag == 4`, and no other cell committed here is
! both. Iodine is the heaviest element with a relativistic PAW dataset here, and
! the small component's norm inside the augmentation sphere is 1e-4 of the large
! one's, so this is where the term is largest.
!
! A neutral iodine atom is 5s2 5p5, one hole in the p shell, so it carries a
! moment of one Bohr magneton, and `occupations = 'fixed'` with nbnd = 8 keeps
! seven filled spinor bands and one empty -- the same construction as
! `i-atom-soc.in`, whose header explains why a smearing wide enough to converge
! an isolated atom would destroy the manifold.
!
! The box is 9 bohr and the cutoffs are 25/200 rather than `i-atom-soc.in`'s 12
! bohr and 45, and `conv_thr` is 1e-8 rather than 1e-10. That is deliberate and
! it is about the *reference*: at 1e-10 in a 12 bohr box `pw.x` is still at
! 3e-9 after 80 iterations on this cell, because an isolated magnetic atom with
! fixed occupations is a soft surface, and a comparison whose reference did not
! converge is worth nothing. At these settings both codes converge.
 &control
    calculation = 'scf'
 /
 &system
    ibrav = 1, celldm(1) = 9.0, nat = 1, ntyp = 1,
    ecutwfc = 25.0, ecutrho = 200.0,
    occupations = 'fixed', nbnd = 8, nosym = .true., noinv = .true.,
    noncolin = .true., lspinorb = .true.,
    starting_magnetization(1) = 0.5, angle1(1) = 0.0
 /
 &electrons
    conv_thr = 1.0d-8, mixing_beta = 0.3
 /
ATOMIC_SPECIES
 I 126.9 I.rel-pbe-n-kjpaw_psl.1.0.0.UPF
ATOMIC_POSITIONS crystal
 I 0.00 0.00 0.00
K_POINTS (automatic)
 1 1 1 0 0 0
